+## Refusals
+
+When auto mode refuses a command, use the alternative here once. A second refusal is a stop.
+Record each refusal in the PR: the command, the reason shown, and what you did.
+
+| Refused in the log | This pass |
+| --- | --- |
+| `kill`, `pkill`, `claude stop` (Interfere With Workloads) | Never type them. Stop a background command with `TaskStop`. |
+| `git commit --no-verify` (Safety Bypass Flag) | Never. Fix what the hook reports and commit again. |
+| An edit to `claude/.claude/settings.json`, or `stow` (Self-Modification) | Outside this pass. A task that seems to need one is a stop. |
+| A compound command the classifier refused with no reason, or while it was unavailable | Re-issue the same work as single commands, each run from the worktree with no `cd` and no pipe. |
+| `git push origin HEAD:main` (unexplained classifier) | Push only the pass branch: `git push -u origin ur-w2`, as its own command. Never push to `main`. |
+| `gh pr merge`, a `gh pr checks --watch` chained to a merge (Merge Without Review) | Never merge. The executor ends when the PR is ready. |
+| A `grep` over session transcripts in `~/.claude/projects` (PII Data Handling) | Never read another session's transcript. Every fact this pass needs is in this plan or the repo. |
+| `cairn-run-gate '<string>'` in a worktree | `bash scripts/gate.sh`, and `bash scripts/gate.sh --scope-changed` for the fast lane. Never pipe either into `tail` or `head`. |
