+## Refusals
+
+| Command | Rule |
+| --- | --- |
+| `kill`, `pkill`, `claude stop` | Never. Stop a background command with `TaskStop`. |
+| `git commit --no-verify` | Never. Fix what the hook reports. |
+| An edit to a setting, a hook registration, a permission rule, or an auto-mode entry, or `stow` | Outside this pass. Needing one is a stop. |
+| A skill file edited from Bash (a heredoc, `sed -i`, a Python one-liner) | Never. Use the Edit and Write tools. |
+| A compound command auto mode refuses | Run its parts as single commands, with no `cd` and no pipe. |
+| A push | Only `git push -u origin ur-w4`. Never to `main`, never forced. |
+| A merge, or any `approval-queue` command | Never. The conductor's. |
+| A read of a transcript under `~/.claude/projects` | Never. |
+| `cairn-run-gate '<string>'` | Use `bash scripts/gate.sh`. |
+| `notify-send` | Never. |
